==Finnish==
{{Finnish index|k|a}}

===Etymology===
Possibly an ancient loan from {{etyl|ine-pro|fi}} {{term/t|ine-pro|*h₂ewks-e/o-}} (from {{term/t|ine-pro|*h₂ewg-||to grow}}), with metathesis from ''*kawsa-'' to {{etyl|fiu-fin-pro|fi}} {{term/t|fiu-fin-pro|*kasva-}} (whence also e.g. Estonian {{term|kasuda|lang=et}}, Livonian {{term|ka'zzõ|lang=liv}}, Votic {{term|kazvaa|lang=vot}}). The loan is shared with the Mordvinic languages (e.g. Erzya {{term|касомс|tr=kasoms|lang=myv}}).

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|lang=fi|/ˈkɑsvɑː(ʔ)/}}
* Rhymes: [[rasvaa]]
* {{hyphenation|kas|vaa}}

===Verb===
{{fi-verb}}
{{context|intransitive|lang=fi}} 

# to [[grow]]
# ''~ [[aikuinen|aikuiseksi]]'': to [[grow up]]
# to [[increase]], [[increment]]
# to [[wax]] {{gloss|of the Moon}}

